  "method": {
    "waveform": "Mean of stereo decoded float PCM. No gain normalization, EQ, pitch shifting or alignment. Only constant and linear terms in harmonic regression remove nuisance offset/trend.",
    "harmonic_regression": "Least squares at every fourth sample: constant, centered time, cosine and sine for harmonics1..12. Period-identification rows optimize high-octave base frequency76..79Hz then use its half-frequency for odd/even harmonic energies. Temporal rows optimize fundamental +/-3% from nominal over note+30ms to note-off-20ms.",
    "period_metric": "For each independent hardware-only segment, subtract mean, search integer lag +/-1.5% around sr/77.3 or sr/38.65; minimize mean((x[:-lag]-x[lag:])^2)/(mean(x[:-lag]^2)+mean(x[lag:]^2)).",
    "temporal_windows": "Early note-on+[35,115]ms, late note-off- [105,25]ms. Repeat both windows shifted -25,0,+25ms. Septum windows additionally include its retained93samples latency.",
    "harmonic_change": "20log10((H3/H1)_late/(H3/H1)_early), analogousH6. Fixed gain and linear time-invariant recording response cancel approximately for locally stationary same-frequency harmonic ratios over time; dynamic processing does not.",
    "environment": "Python3.11, numpy1.26.4, scipy1.14.1"
  },
  "conclusions": [
    "Three roughly90ms high Eb notes are missing from baseline Moogie reconstruction; their pitch periods and suppressed odd harmonics match an already-transcribed high Eb. Corrected variant retains uncertainty and does not overwrite baseline.",
    "Hardware within-note harmonic balance evolves substantially more than baseline render for these held low Eb notes; a fixed EQ/level adjustment cannot explain this alone. This does not identify a unique filter, envelope or oscillator-phase cause."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Original keyboard events and recording chain are unavailable. High-note timing remains approximately20ms uncertain; note-offs meet following note-on by assumption.",
    "The octave inference is strongly supported by independent periodicity, harmonic suppression and three repeated phrase locations. A contrived coordinated waveform/controller change cannot be logically excluded without original MIDI.",
    "The temporal comparison uses existing baseline renders only; corrected reconstruction must be rendered separately before making whole-excerpt conclusions.",
    "Velocity sensitivity and relative oscillator phase, filter/envelope scaling, time-varying capture processing and undisclosed controllers remain relevant to timbral interpretation."
  ]
